{"task_id": "HumanEval/6", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List\n\ndef parse_nested_parens(paren_string: str) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Parses a string of space-separated parentheses groups to find the deepest nesting level for each.\n    This function handles multiple groups and returns their nesting levels.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _calculate_deepest_nesting(group: str) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Calculates the deepest nesting level for a single, valid parentheses group string.\n        It assumes the input group is balanced and well-formed.\n        \"\"\"\n        current_max = 0\n        current_depth = 0\n        for char in group:\n            if char == '(':\n                current_depth += 1\n                current_max = max(current_max, current_depth)\n            elif char == ')':\n                current_depth -= 1\n        return current_max\n\n    if not paren_string.strip():\n        return []\n\n    groups = paren_string.split(' ')\n    results = []\n    for group in groups:\n        if group:\n            results.append(_calculate_deepest_nesting(group))\n    return results\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/8", "solution": "from typing import List, Tuple\n\n\ndef sum_product(numbers: List[int]) -> Tuple[int, int]:\n    \"\"\" For a given list of integers, return a tuple consisting of a sum and a product of all the integers in a list.\n    Empty sum should be equal to 0 and empty product should be equal to 1.\n    \"\"\"\n    current_sum = 0\n    current_product = 1\n\n    for number in numbers:\n        current_sum += number\n        current_product *= number\n\n    return (current_sum, current_product)"}
