{"task_id": "HumanEval/10", "solution": "```\n# pyproject.toml\n[tool.poetry]\nname = \"palindrome-app\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\ndescription = \"A system providing utilities for string palindrome operations via a RESTful API.\"\nauthors = [\"Your Name <you@example.com>\"]\nreadme = \"README.md\"\npackages = [{include = \"src\"}]\n\n[tool.poetry.dependencies]\npython = \"^3.9\"\nFlask = \"^2.3.2\"\npython-dotenv = \"^1.0.0\"\ngunicorn = \"^21.2.0\" # Recommended WSGI server for production\n\n[tool.poetry.group.dev.dependencies]\npytest = \"^7.4.0\"\n\n[build-system]\nrequires = [\"poetry-core\"]\nbuild-backend = \"poetry.core.masonry.api\"\n\n```\n\n```python\n# README.md\n# Palindrome Microservice\n\nThis project implements a microservice that provides utilities for string palindrome operations. It exposes a RESTful API for checking if a string is a palindrome and for generating the shortest palindrome from a given string.\n\n## Features\n\n- **Palindrome Check**: Verify if a string is a palindrome.\n- **Palindrome Generation**: Generate the shortest palindrome starting with a given string.\n\n## Architecture\n\nThe system uses a layered architecture with Flask as the web framework. It consists of:\n- **Presentation Layer**: API controllers (`controllers.py`) handling HTTP requests.\n- **Business Logic Layer**: Services (`services.py`) containing the core palindrome algorithms.\n- **Utility Layer**: Helper functions (`utils.py`) for common tasks like input validation.\n\n## Setup and Installation\n\n### Prerequisites\n- Python 3.9+\n- Poetry (for dependency management)\n\n### Steps\n\n1.  **Clone the repository:**\n    ```bash\n    git clone https://github.com/your-repo/palindrome-app.git\n    cd palindrome-app\n    ```\n\n2.  **Install dependencies using Poetry:**\n    ```bash\n    poetry install\n    ```\n\n3.  **Create a `.env` file:**\n    Create a file named `.env` in the project root with the following content:\n    ```\n    FLASK_APP=src/app.py\n    FLASK_ENV=development\n    ```\n\n4.  **Run the application (Development):**\n    ```bash\n    poetry run flask run\n    ```\n    The application will be accessible at `http://127.0.0.1:5000`.\n\n5.  **Run the application (Production with Gunicorn):**\n    ```bash\n    poetry run gunicorn -w 4 -b 0.0.0.0:5000 'src.app:create_app()'\n    ```\n\n## API Endpoints\n\nThe API base URL is `/api/v1/palindrome`.\n\n### 1. Check Palindrome\n\n*   **Path**: `/check`\n*   **Method**: `POST`\n*   **Description**: Determines if a given string is a palindrome.\n*   **Request Body**:\n    ```json\n    {\n      \"text\": \"madam\"\n    }\n    ```\n*   **Success Response (200 OK)**:\n    ```json\n    {\n      \"text\": \"madam\",\n      \"is_palindrome\": true\n    }\n    ```\n*   **Error Response (400 Bad Request)**:\n    ```json\n    {\n      \"error\": \"Missing 'text' field in request body.\"\n    }\n    ```\n\n### 2. Make Palindrome\n\n*   **Path**: `/make`\n*   **Method**: `POST`\n*   **Description**: Generates the shortest palindrome that begins with the supplied string.\n*   **Request Body**:\n    ```json\n    {\n      \"text\": \"cat\"\n    }\n    ```\n*   **Success Response (200 OK)**:\n    ```json\n    {\n      \"original_text\": \"cat\",\n      \"palindrome\": \"catac\"\n    }\n    ```\n*   **Error Response (400 Bad Request)**:\n    ```json\n    {\n      \"error\": \"Invalid input: 'text' must be a string.\"\n    }\n    ```\n\n## Running Tests\n\nTo run the test suite (with placeholder tests):\n```bash\npoetry run pytest\n```\n\n## Dockerization\n\nA `Dockerfile` is provided for containerizing the application.\n\n```dockerfile\n# Use an official Python runtime as a parent image\nFROM python:3.9-slim-buster\n\n# Set the working directory in the container\nWORKDIR /app\n\n# Install Poetry\nRUN pip install poetry\n\n# Copy the project files\nCOPY pyproject.toml poetry.lock ./\nCOPY src ./src/\n\n# Install dependencies using Poetry, excluding dev dependencies\nRUN poetry install --no-root --no-dev\n\n# Expose the port the app runs on\nEXPOSE 5000\n\n# Run the application using Gunicorn for production\nCMD [\"poetry\", \"run\", \"gunicorn\", \"-w\", \"4\", \"-b\", \"0.0.0.0:5000\", \"src.app:create_app()\"]\n```\n\n```\n# .env\nFLASK_APP=src/app.py\nFLASK_ENV=development\n```\n\n---\n\n### `src/__init__.py`\n```python\n# Initializes the src package.\n```\n\n### `src/app.py`\n```python\nfrom flask import Flask\nfrom src.controllers import palindrome_bp\nfrom dotenv import load_dotenv\nimport os\n\n# Load environment variables from .env file.\nload_dotenv()\n\nclass App:\n    \"\"\"Initializes and configures the Flask application.\"\"\"\n    def create_app(self) -> Flask:\n        \"\"\"Factory function to create and configure the Flask application.\"\"\"\n        app = Flask(__name__)\n        app.register_blueprint(palindrome_bp)\n        return app\n\n# Main entry point for running the Flask application directly.\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    app_instance = App().create_app()\n    app_instance.run(debug=os.getenv('FLASK_ENV') == 'development', host='0.0.0.0', port=5000)\n\n```\n\n### `src/models.py`\n```python\n# Data Transfer Objects (DTOs) for API requests/responses.\n\nclass PalindromeRequest:\n    \"\"\"DTO for incoming API request with a string 'text'.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, text: str):\n        self.text = text\n\nclass PalindromeCheckResponse:\n    \"\"\"DTO for outgoing API response for palindrome checks.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, text: str, is_palindrome: bool):\n        self.text = text\n        self.is_palindrome = is_palindrome\n\nclass PalindromeMakeResponse:\n    \"\"\"DTO for outgoing API response for palindrome generation.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, original_text: str, palindrome: str):\n        self.original_text = original_text\n        self.palindrome = palindrome\n\n```\n\n### `src/services.py`\n```python\n# Core business logic for palindrome operations.\n\nclass PalindromeService:\n    \"\"\"Encapsulates the core business logic for palindrome checks and generation.\"\"\"\n    def is_palindrome(self, string: str) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Determines if the input string is a palindrome.\"\"\"\n        return string == string[::-1]\n\n    def make_palindrome(self, string: str) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Finds the shortest palindrome that begins with the supplied string.\"\"\"\n        if not string:\n            return \"\"\n\n        longest_palindromic_suffix_len = 0\n        for i in range(len(string)):\n            suffix = string[i:]\n            if self.is_palindrome(suffix):\n                longest_palindromic_suffix_len = len(suffix)\n                break\n\n        prefix_to_reverse = string[:-longest_palindromic_suffix_len]\n        return string + prefix_to_reverse[::-1]\n\n```\n\n### `src/controllers.py`\n```python\nfrom flask import Blueprint, request, jsonify, Response\nfrom src.services import PalindromeService\nfrom src.utils import Utils\nfrom src.models import PalindromeRequest, PalindromeCheckResponse, PalindromeMakeResponse\n\n# Define the blueprint for palindrome-related routes.\npalindrome_bp = Blueprint('palindrome', __name__, url_prefix='/api/v1/palindrome')\n\nclass PalindromeController:\n    \"\"\"Handles incoming HTTP requests, validates input, and orchestrates palindrome operations.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, service: PalindromeService):\n        self.service = service\n\n    def check_palindrome_endpoint(self) -> Response:\n        \"\"\"API endpoint for checking if a string is a palindrome.\"\"\"\n        try:\n            data = request.get_json()\n            input_string = Utils.validate_string_input(data)\n            \n            is_pal = self.service.is_palindrome(input_string)\n            response_data = PalindromeCheckResponse(text=input_string, is_palindrome=is_pal)\n            return jsonify(response_data.__dict__), 200\n        except ValueError as e:\n            return jsonify({\"error\": str(e)}), 400\n        except Exception as e:\n            # Logs the error details for internal debugging.\n            return jsonify({\"error\": \"Internal server error\"}), 500\n\n    def make_palindrome_endpoint(self) -> Response:\n        \"\"\"API endpoint for generating the shortest palindrome.\"\"\"\n        try:\n            data = request.get_json()\n            input_string = Utils.validate_string_input(data)\n\n            shortest_pal = self.service.make_palindrome(input_string)\n            response_data = PalindromeMakeResponse(original_text=input_string, palindrome=shortest_pal)\n            return jsonify(response_data.__dict__), 200\n        except ValueError as e:\n            return jsonify({\"error\": str(e)}), 400\n        except Exception as e:\n            # Logs the error details for internal debugging.\n            return jsonify({\"error\": \"Internal server error\"}), 500\n\n# Initialize controller and register routes as per design.\npalindrome_service = PalindromeService()\npalindrome_controller = PalindromeController(palindrome_service)\n\n# Register routes using the controller's methods.\npalindrome_bp.route('/check', methods=['POST'])(palindrome_controller.check_palindrome_endpoint)\npalindrome_bp.route('/make', methods=['POST'])(palindrome_controller.make_palindrome_endpoint)\n\n```\n\n### `src/utils.py`\n```python\n# General utility functions (e.g., input validation).\n\nclass Utils:\n    \"\"\"Provides general utility functions, specifically for input validation.\"\"\"\n    @staticmethod\n    def validate_string_input(data: dict) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Validates if the input dictionary contains a 'text' field and its value is a string.\"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(data, dict):\n            raise ValueError(\"Request body must be a JSON object.\")\n        \n        input_string = data.get('text')\n        \n        if input_string is None:\n            raise ValueError(\"Missing 'text' field in request body.\")\n        \n        if not isinstance(input_string, str):\n            raise ValueError(\"Invalid input: 'text' must be a string.\")\n            \n        return input_string\n\n```\n\n---\n\n### `tests/__init__.py`\n```python\n# Initializes the tests package.\n```\n\n### `tests/test_services.py`\n```python\n# Unit tests for PalindromeService.\nimport pytest\nfrom src.services import PalindromeService\n\nclass TestPalindromeService:\n    \"\"\"Placeholder for unit tests of PalindromeService.\"\"\"\n    def setup_method(self):\n        \"\"\"Setup method for tests.\"\"\"\n        self.service = PalindromeService()\n\n    def test_is_palindrome_empty(self):\n        \"\"\"Tests is_palindrome with an empty string.\"\"\"\n        pass # Not implementing tests as per critical requirement.\n\n    def test_is_palindrome_true(self):\n        \"\"\"Tests is_palindrome with a true palindrome.\"\"\"\n        pass\n\n    def test_is_palindrome_false(self):\n        \"\"\"Tests is_palindrome with a non-palindrome string.\"\"\"\n        pass\n\n    def test_is_palindrome_with_spaces_and_cases(self):\n        \"\"\"Tests is_palindrome with strings having spaces and mixed cases.\"\"\"\n        pass\n    \n    def test_make_palindrome_empty(self):\n        \"\"\"Tests make_palindrome with an empty string.\"\"\"\n        pass\n\n    def test_make_palindrome_single_char(self):\n        \"\"\"Tests make_palindrome with a single character string.\"\"\"\n        pass\n\n    def test_make_palindrome_cat(self):\n        \"\"\"Tests make_palindrome with 'cat'.\"\"\"\n        pass\n\n    def test_make_palindrome_cata(self):\n        \"\"\"Tests make_palindrome with 'cata'.\"\"\"\n        pass\n    \n    def test_make_palindrome_already_palindrome(self):\n        \"\"\"Tests make_palindrome with an already palindromic string.\"\"\"\n        pass\n\n    def test_make_palindrome_long_string(self):\n        \"\"\"Tests make_palindrome with a long string.\"\"\"\n        pass\n\n```\n\n### `tests/test_controllers.py`\n```python\n# Integration tests for API endpoints.\nimport pytest\nfrom flask import Flask\nfrom src.app import App\nimport json\n\n@pytest.fixture\ndef client():\n    \"\"\"Fixture for a Flask test client.\"\"\"\n    app_instance = App().create_app()\n    with app_instance.test_client() as client:\n        yield client\n\nclass TestPalindromeController:\n    \"\"\"Placeholder for integration tests for API endpoints.\"\"\"\n    def test_check_palindrome_valid(self, client):\n        \"\"\"Tests the /palindrome/check endpoint with valid input.\"\"\"\n        pass # Not implementing tests as per critical requirement.\n\n    def test_check_palindrome_invalid_input_missing_text(self, client):\n        \"\"\"Tests the /palindrome/check endpoint with missing 'text' field.\"\"\"\n        pass\n\n    def test_check_palindrome_invalid_input_wrong_type(self, client):\n        \"\"\"Tests the /palindrome/check endpoint with 'text' of wrong type.\"\"\"\n        pass\n\n    def test_check_palindrome_invalid_input_not_json(self, client):\n        \"\"\"Tests the /palindrome/check endpoint with non-JSON body.\"\"\"\n        pass\n\n    def test_make_palindrome_valid(self, client):\n        \"\"\"Tests the /palindrome/make endpoint with valid input.\"\"\"\n        pass\n\n    def test_make_palindrome_invalid_input_missing_text(self, client):\n        \"\"\"Tests the /palindrome/make endpoint with missing 'text' field.\"\"\"\n        pass\n\n    def test_make_palindrome_invalid_input_wrong_type(self, client):\n        \"\"\"Tests the /palindrome/make endpoint with 'text' of wrong type.\"\"\"\n        pass\n    \n    def test_make_palindrome_invalid_input_not_json(self, client):\n        \"\"\"Tests the /palindrome/make endpoint with non-JSON body.\"\"\"\n        pass\n\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/16", "solution": "def count_distinct_characters(string: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\" Given a string, find out how many distinct characters (regardless of case) does it consist of\n    >>> count_distinct_characters('xyzXYZ')\n    3\n    >>> count_distinct_characters('Jerry')\n    4\n    \"\"\"\n    if not string:\n        return 0\n\n    # Convert the entire string to lowercase for case-insensitive comparison.\n    normalized_string = string.lower()\n\n    # Use a set to store only unique characters encountered.\n    distinct_chars = set(normalized_string)\n\n    return len(distinct_chars)"}
