{"task_id": "HumanEval/32", "solution": "import math\n\n\ndef poly(xs: list, x: float):\n    \"\"\"Evaluates polynomial with coefficients xs at point x.\n    return xs[0] + xs[1] * x + xs[2] * x^2 + .... xs[n] * x^n\n    \"\"\"\n    return sum([coeff * math.pow(x, i) for i, coeff in enumerate(xs)])\n\n\ndef find_zero(xs: list):\n    \"\"\"Finds x such that poly(x) = 0 using bisection method.\n    It takes list xs having even number of coefficients and a non-zero leading coefficient.\n    \"\"\"\n    DEFAULT_TOLERANCE = 1e-6\n    DEFAULT_MAX_ITERATIONS = 1000\n    DEFAULT_SEARCH_RANGE = (-100.0, 100.0)\n\n    func = lambda val: poly(xs, val)\n    a, b = DEFAULT_SEARCH_RANGE\n\n    # For odd-degree polynomials with real coefficients, a root is guaranteed.\n    # We assume func(a) and func(b) will have opposite signs in the search range.\n    \n    # Check for exact roots at the initial interval boundaries.\n    if func(a) == 0:\n        return a\n    if func(b) == 0:\n        return b\n\n    for _ in range(DEFAULT_MAX_ITERATIONS):\n        mid = (a + b) / 2\n        \n        # If the value at mid is within tolerance of zero, return mid.\n        if abs(func(mid)) < DEFAULT_TOLERANCE:\n            return mid\n        \n        # Narrow the search interval based on the sign change.\n        if func(a) * func(mid) < 0:\n            b = mid\n        else:\n            a = mid\n            \n    # If the root is not found within max_iterations, return the last midpoint.\n    # Error handling for non-convergence or invalid range is explicitly forbidden.\n    return (a + b) / 2"}
