{"task_id": "HumanEval/32", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef poly(xs: list, x: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Evaluates polynomial with coefficients xs at point x.\n    Returns xs[0] + xs[1] * x + xs[2] * x^2 + .... xs[n] * x^n.\n    \"\"\"\n    return sum([coeff * math.pow(x, i) for i, coeff in enumerate(xs)])\n\ndef find_zero(xs: list) -> float:\n    \"\"\"find_zero finds x such that poly(x) = 0.\n    It returns one zero for polynomials with an even number of coefficients, assuming a solution exists and converges.\n    \"\"\"\n    max_iterations = 1000\n    tolerance = 1e-6\n\n    def derivative_poly(coeffs: list, val: float) -> float:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the derivative of the polynomial at a given value.\"\"\"\n        return sum([i * coeff * math.pow(val, i - 1) for i, coeff in enumerate(coeffs) if i > 0])\n\n    x0 = 0.0\n    # Attempt a slightly better initial guess if possible, assuming xs has at least 2 coefficients\n    if len(xs) > 1 and xs[1] != 0:\n        x0 = -xs[0] / xs[1]\n\n    for _ in range(max_iterations):\n        y = poly(xs, x0)\n        \n        if abs(y) < tolerance:\n            return x0\n\n        y_prime = derivative_poly(xs, x0)\n\n        # If derivative is too small, the method is unstable.\n        # Since exceptions are forbidden, return current best guess.\n        if abs(y_prime) < tolerance:\n            return x0\n\n        x_new = x0 - y / y_prime\n        \n        if abs(x_new - x0) < tolerance:\n            return x_new\n        \n        x0 = x_new\n    \n    # If the loop finishes without converging, return the last calculated value as the best effort.\n    return x0\n```"}
