{"task_id": "HumanEval/49", "solution": "```python\ndef modp(n: int, p: int):\n    \"\"\"Return 2^n modulo p (be aware of numerics).\n    >>> modp(3, 5)\n    3\n    >>> modp(1101, 101)\n    2\n    >>> modp(0, 101)\n    1\n    >>> modp(3, 11)\n    8\n    >>> modp(100, 101)\n    1\n    \"\"\"\n    # Assuming n >= 0 and p > 0 based on critical requirements\n    # \"Do NOT add isinstance() checks, type guards, or raise exceptions for edge cases.\n    # Trust the caller's inputs and implement the simplest, most direct logic possible.\"\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1 % p\n\n    result = 1\n    base = 2 % p\n\n    while n > 0:\n        if n % 2 == 1:\n            result = (result * base) % p\n        base = (base * base) % p\n        n //= 2\n\n    return result\n```"}
