{"task_id": "HumanEval/86", "solution": "```python\ndef anti_shuffle(s):\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts characters within each word of a string based on ASCII values.\n    Maintains original word order and spacing, treating contiguous non-space sequences as words.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not s:\n        return \"\"\n\n    result_parts = []\n    current_segment = []\n    \n    # Initialize based on the first character\n    is_current_segment_space = s[0].isspace()\n    current_segment.append(s[0])\n\n    # Parse string into segments of words or spaces\n    for char in s[1:]:\n        char_is_space = char.isspace()\n\n        if char_is_space == is_current_segment_space:\n            current_segment.append(char)\n        else:\n            result_parts.append(\"\".join(current_segment))\n            current_segment = [char]\n            is_current_segment_space = char_is_space\n    \n    # Add the last segment\n    result_parts.append(\"\".join(current_segment))\n\n    # Process segments: sort words, preserve spaces\n    final_string_parts = []\n    for part in result_parts:\n        if part.isspace():\n            final_string_parts.append(part)\n        else:\n            final_string_parts.append(\"\".join(sorted(part))) # Inlined sort word logic\n\n    return \"\".join(final_string_parts)\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/86", "solution": "```python\ndef anti_shuffle(s):\n    \"\"\"\n    Takes a string and returns an ordered version of it.\n    Words are replaced by a new word where characters are arranged in ascending ASCII order.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not s:\n        return s\n\n    result_parts = []\n    current_word = []\n    \n    for char in s:\n        if char == ' ':\n            if current_word:\n                # Sort characters within the accumulated word\n                result_parts.append(\"\".join(sorted(\"\".join(current_word))))\n                current_word = []\n            result_parts.append(' ')\n        else:\n            current_word.append(char)\n    \n    # Handle the last word if the string doesn't end with a space\n    if current_word:\n        result_parts.append(\"\".join(sorted(\"\".join(current_word))))\n        \n    return \"\".join(result_parts)\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/89", "solution": "def encrypt(s):\n    \"\"\"Create a function encrypt that takes a string as an argument and\n    returns a string encrypted with the alphabet being rotated.\n    \"\"\"\n    SHIFT_AMOUNT = 4\n    LOWER_A_ORD = ord('a')\n    LOWER_Z_ORD = ord('z')\n    UPPER_A_ORD = ord('A')\n    UPPER_Z_ORD = ord('Z')\n\n    result_chars = []\n\n    for char in s:\n        char_ord = ord(char)\n        if LOWER_A_ORD <= char_ord <= LOWER_Z_ORD:\n            # Handle lowercase letters\n            shifted_ord = LOWER_A_ORD + (char_ord - LOWER_A_ORD + SHIFT_AMOUNT) % (LOWER_Z_ORD - LOWER_A_ORD + 1)\n            result_chars.append(chr(shifted_ord))\n        elif UPPER_A_ORD <= char_ord <= UPPER_Z_ORD:\n            # Handle uppercase letters\n            shifted_ord = UPPER_A_ORD + (char_ord - UPPER_A_ORD + SHIFT_AMOUNT) % (UPPER_Z_ORD - UPPER_A_ORD + 1)\n            result_chars.append(chr(shifted_ord))\n        else:\n            # Non-alphabetic characters remain unchanged\n            result_chars.append(char)\n\n    return \"\".join(result_chars)"}
