{"task_id": "HumanEval/96", "solution": "def count_up_to(n):\n    \"\"\"Returns a list of all prime numbers strictly less than n.\n    Implements trial division for primality testing.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 2:\n        return []\n\n    primes = []\n    for num in range(2, n):\n        is_prime = True\n        # Check for divisors from 2 up to the square root of num.\n        for i in range(2, int(num**0.5) + 1):\n            if num % i == 0:\n                is_prime = False\n                break\n        if is_prime:\n            primes.append(num)\n    return primes"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/96", "solution": "def count_up_to(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates all prime numbers strictly less than n using the Sieve of Eratosthenes.\n    Returns an empty list if n is 0, 1, or 2.\n    \"\"\"\n    # As per critical requirements, no input validation is performed.\n    # 'n' is assumed to be a non-negative integer.\n\n    if n <= 2:\n        return []\n\n    primes = []\n    # Initialize a boolean array 'is_prime_sieve' marking potential primes.\n    is_prime_sieve = [True] * n\n    is_prime_sieve[0] = is_prime_sieve[1] = False # 0 and 1 are not prime numbers.\n\n    # Iterate through numbers from 2 up to n-1.\n    for p in range(2, n):\n        # If 'p' is marked as true, it is a prime number.\n        if is_prime_sieve[p]:\n            primes.append(p)\n            # Mark all multiples of 'p' (starting from p*p) as not prime.\n            # Multiples less than p*p would have already been marked by smaller primes.\n            for multiple in range(p * p, n, p):\n                is_prime_sieve[multiple] = False\n    return primes"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/95", "solution": "```python\ndef check_dict_case(dict):\n    \"\"\"\n    Given a dictionary, return True if all keys are strings in lower \n    case or all keys are strings in upper case, else return False.\n    Returns False if the given dictionary is empty or contains non-string keys.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not dict:\n        return False\n\n    all_lower_case = True\n    all_upper_case = True\n\n    for key in dict.keys():\n        if not isinstance(key, str):\n            return False\n            \n        if not key.islower():\n            all_lower_case = False\n            \n        if not key.isupper():\n            all_upper_case = False\n            \n        # Early exit if both flags are false, indicating a mix of cases\n        if not all_lower_case and not all_upper_case:\n            return False\n\n    return all_lower_case or all_upper_case\n\n```"}
