{"task_id": "HumanEval/99", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef closest_integer(value):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the closest integer to a given number string,\n    rounding away from zero if equidistant.\n    \"\"\"\n    num = float(value)\n\n    floor_val = math.floor(num)\n    ceil_val = math.ceil(num)\n\n    dist_to_floor = abs(num - floor_val)\n    dist_to_ceil = abs(num - ceil_val)\n\n    if dist_to_floor == dist_to_ceil:\n        # Equidistant, round away from zero.\n        # This means returning the integer with the larger absolute value.\n        return int(ceil_val) if num >= 0 else int(floor_val)\n    elif dist_to_floor < dist_to_ceil:\n        # Closer to floor_val.\n        return int(floor_val)\n    else:\n        # Closer to ceil_val.\n        return int(ceil_val)\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/100", "solution": "def make_a_pile(n: int) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the number of stones for each of `n` levels in a pile.\n    The first level has `n` stones, and subsequent levels increase by 2, maintaining the parity of `n`.\"\"\"\n    pile = [n]\n    current_stones = n\n    for _ in range(1, n):\n        current_stones += 2\n        pile.append(current_stones)\n    return pile"}
