{"task_id": "HumanEval/126", "solution": "def is_sorted(lst):\n    \"\"\"\n    Given a list of numbers, return whether or not they are sorted\n    in ascending order. If list has more than 1 duplicate of the same\n    number, return False.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(lst) <= 1:\n        return True\n\n    # Check for ascending order\n    for i in range(len(lst) - 1):\n        if lst[i] > lst[i+1]:\n            return False\n\n    # Check for duplicate rule (no number appears more than twice)\n    counts = {}\n    for item in lst:\n        counts[item] = counts.get(item, 0) + 1\n\n    for count in counts.values():\n        if count > 2:\n            return False\n\n    return True"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/127", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef intersection(interval1, interval2):\n    \"\"\"Determines whether the length of intersection of two intervals is a prime number.\n    Returns \"YES\" if prime, \"NO\" otherwise or if intervals don't intersect.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def is_prime(n: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Checks if a non-negative integer n is a prime number.\n        Implements the primality test as specified in FR3.\n        \"\"\"\n        if n <= 1:\n            return False\n        if n == 2:\n            return True\n        if n % 2 == 0:\n            return False\n        for i in range(3, int(math.sqrt(n)) + 1, 2):\n            if n % i == 0:\n                return False\n        return True\n\n    # Parse input intervals\n    start1, end1 = interval1\n    start2, end2 = interval2\n\n    # FR1: Calculate the intersection of two closed integer intervals.\n    max_start = max(start1, start2)\n    min_end = min(end1, end2)\n\n    # FR5: Return \"NO\" if the two intervals do not intersect.\n    if max_start > min_end:\n        return \"NO\"\n    else:\n        # Intersection exists: (max_start, min_end)\n\n        # FR2: Calculate the length of the intersection interval.\n        length = min_end - max_start + 1\n\n        # FR4: Determine if the length is a prime number and return \"YES\" or \"NO\".\n        if is_prime(length):\n            return \"YES\"\n        else:\n            return \"NO\"\n\n```"}
