{"task_id": "HumanEval/128", "solution": "```python\ndef prod_signs(arr):\n    \"\"\"\n    You are given an array arr of integers and you need to return\n    sum of magnitudes of integers multiplied by product of all signs\n    of each number in the array, represented by 1, -1 or 0.\n    Note: return None for empty arr.\n\n    Example:\n    >>> prod_signs([1, 2, 2, -4]) == -9\n    >>> prod_signs([0, 1]) == 0\n    >>> prod_signs([]) == None\n    \"\"\"\n    if not arr:\n        return None\n\n    product_of_signs = 1\n    sum_of_magnitudes = 0\n\n    for num in arr:\n        current_sign = 0\n        if num > 0:\n            current_sign = 1\n        elif num < 0:\n            current_sign = -1\n        # If num == 0, current_sign remains 0.\n\n        product_of_signs *= current_sign\n        sum_of_magnitudes += abs(num)\n\n    return sum_of_magnitudes * product_of_signs\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/127", "solution": "def intersection(interval1, interval2):\n    \"\"\"Determines whether the length of intersection of two intervals is a prime number.\n    Returns \"YES\" if the length is prime, otherwise \"NO\".\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _is_prime(number):\n        \"\"\"Checks if a given number is prime.\"\"\"\n        if number <= 1:\n            return False\n        if number <= 3:\n            return True\n        if number % 2 == 0 or number % 3 == 0:\n            return False\n\n        i = 5\n        while i * i <= number:\n            if number % i == 0 or number % (i + 2) == 0:\n                return False\n            i += 6\n        return True\n\n    int1_start, int1_end = interval1\n    int2_start, int2_end = interval2\n\n    intersection_start = max(int1_start, int2_start)\n    intersection_end = min(int1_end, int2_end)\n\n    if intersection_start > intersection_end:\n        return \"NO\"\n\n    length = intersection_end - intersection_start\n\n    if _is_prime(length):\n        return \"YES\"\n    else:\n        return \"NO\""}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/130", "solution": "```python\ndef tri(n):\n    \"\"\"Calculates the first n + 1 numbers of the Tribonacci sequence.\n    This function uses memoization to efficiently compute terms, including forward references.\n    \"\"\"\n    memo = {}\n\n    def get_tribonacci_term(k):\n        if k in memo:\n            return memo[k]\n\n        if k == 0:\n            result = 1\n        elif k == 1:\n            result = 3\n        elif k % 2 == 0:  # k is even and k > 1\n            result = 1 + k // 2\n        else:  # k is odd and k > 1\n            result = (\n                get_tribonacci_term(k - 1)\n                + get_tribonacci_term(k - 2)\n                + get_tribonacci_term(k + 1)\n            )\n\n        memo[k] = result\n        return result\n\n    sequence = []\n    for i in range(n + 1):\n        sequence.append(get_tribonacci_term(i))\n\n    return sequence\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/131", "solution": "```python\ndef digits(n):\n    \"\"\"Given a positive integer n, return the product of the odd digits.\n    Return 0 if all digits are even.\n    For example:\n    digits(1)  == 1\n    digits(4)  == 0\n    digits(235) == 15\n    \"\"\"\n    \n    product = 1\n    found_odd_digit = False\n    \n    # Iterate through digits by converting n to string.\n    for char_digit in str(n):\n        digit = int(char_digit)\n        if digit % 2 != 0:  # If the digit is odd.\n            product *= digit\n            found_odd_digit = True\n    \n    return product if found_odd_digit else 0\n```"}
