{"task_id": "HumanEval/148", "solution": "PLANET_ORDER = [\n    \"Mercury\", \"Venus\", \"Earth\", \"Mars\", \"Jupiter\", \"Saturn\", \"Uranus\", \"Neptune\"\n]\n\ndef bf(planet1, planet2):\n    '''\n    Returns a tuple of planets located between planet1 and planet2, sorted by proximity to the Sun.\n    Returns an empty tuple if either input planet name is incorrect.\n    '''\n    if planet1 not in PLANET_ORDER or planet2 not in PLANET_ORDER:\n        return ()\n\n    idx1 = PLANET_ORDER.index(planet1)\n    idx2 = PLANET_ORDER.index(planet2)\n\n    start_idx = min(idx1, idx2)\n    end_idx = max(idx1, idx2)\n\n    intermediate_planets = PLANET_ORDER[start_idx + 1:end_idx]\n\n    return tuple(intermediate_planets)"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/147", "solution": "```python\ndef get_max_triples(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts triples (a[i], a[j], a[k]) from array a where i < j < k and their sum is a multiple of 3.\n    Array a is defined by a[i] = i*i - i + 1 for 1 <= i <= n.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def nCr_local(n_val, r_val):\n        \"\"\"Calculates 'n choose r', the number of combinations.\"\"\"\n        if r_val < 0 or r_val > n_val:\n            return 0\n        if r_val == 0 or r_val == n_val:\n            return 1\n        if r_val > n_val // 2:\n            r_val = n_val - r_val\n        \n        res = 1\n        for i in range(r_val):\n            res = res * (n_val - i) // (i + 1)\n        return res\n\n    count_mod_0 = 0\n    count_mod_1 = 0\n\n    # The value a[i] = i*i - i + 1. Its remainder modulo 3 depends on i modulo 3.\n    # If i % 3 == 0 or i % 3 == 1, then a[i] % 3 == 1.\n    # If i % 3 == 2, then a[i] % 3 == 0.\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        if i % 3 == 2:\n            count_mod_0 += 1\n        else:\n            count_mod_1 += 1\n    \n    # A sum (a[i] + a[j] + a[k]) is a multiple of 3 if and only if\n    # (a[i]%3 + a[j]%3 + a[k]%3) % 3 == 0.\n    # Given that a[x]%3 can only be 0 or 1, the only ways to sum to 0 (mod 3) are:\n    # (0, 0, 0) or (1, 1, 1).\n    triples_from_mod_0 = nCr_local(count_mod_0, 3)\n    triples_from_mod_1 = nCr_local(count_mod_1, 3)\n\n    return triples_from_mod_0 + triples_from_mod_1\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/145", "solution": "def order_by_points(nums):\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a list of integers by the sum of their digits,\n    then by their original index for tie-breaking.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _calculate_digit_sum(n: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the sum of the absolute digits of an integer.\n        Example: _calculate_digit_sum(-12) == 3.\"\"\"\n        return sum(int(digit) for digit in str(abs(n)))\n\n    decorated_list = []\n    for original_index, num in enumerate(nums):\n        digit_sum = _calculate_digit_sum(num)\n        # Store (digit_sum, original_index, original_number) for sorting\n        decorated_list.append((digit_sum, original_index, num))\n\n    # Sort the decorated list. Python's sort on tuples uses elements sequentially.\n    # First by digit_sum (ascending), then by original_index (ascending).\n    decorated_list.sort()\n\n    # Extract the original numbers in the new sorted order\n    return [item[2] for item in decorated_list]"}
