{"task_id": "HumanEval/150", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef x_or_y(n, x, y):\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns the value of x if n is a prime number, and y otherwise.\n    This function includes the prime checking logic internally.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def is_prime_internal(num):\n        # Checks if a given integer is a prime number.\n        # Assumes 'num' is an integer based on critical requirements.\n        if num <= 1:\n            return False\n        if num == 2:\n            return True\n        if num % 2 == 0:\n            return False\n        for i in range(3, int(math.sqrt(num)) + 1, 2):\n            if num % i == 0:\n                return False\n        return True\n\n    if is_prime_internal(n):\n        return x\n    else:\n        return y\n```"}
