{"task_id": "HumanEval/151", "solution": "def double_the_difference(lst):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of squares of odd, positive integers in a list.\n    Ignores non-integer, negative, or even numbers.\n    \"\"\"\n    total_sum = 0\n\n    if not lst:\n        return 0\n\n    for num in lst:\n        # Check if the number represents an integer value. This handles floats like 3.0 correctly.\n        # We assume numeric types based on \"trust the caller's inputs\" to avoid ValueError from int().\n        if num == int(num):\n            num_as_int = int(num) # Convert to integer for precise calculations and checks.\n            # Only consider numbers that are strictly positive and odd.\n            if num_as_int > 0 and num_as_int % 2 != 0:\n                total_sum += num_as_int * num_as_int\n    return total_sum"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/153", "solution": "```python\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\n\n@dataclass\nclass Extension:\n    \"\"\"Represents an extension with its name and calculated strength.\"\"\"\n    name: str\n    strength: int\n\nclass ExtensionStrengthCalculator:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the strength of a single extension string.\"\"\"\n    def calculate(self, extension_name: str) -> int:\n        cap_count = sum(1 for char in extension_name if char.isupper())\n        sm_count = sum(1 for char in extension_name if char.islower())\n        return cap_count - sm_count\n\nclass StrongestExtensionFinder:\n    \"\"\"Finds the strongest extension from a list based on calculated strengths.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, calculator: ExtensionStrengthCalculator):\n        self._calculator = calculator\n\n    def find(self, extensions: list[str]) -> Extension:\n        strongest_ext: Extension | None = None\n\n        for ext_name in extensions:\n            current_strength = self._calculator.calculate(ext_name)\n            current_ext = Extension(name=ext_name, strength=current_strength)\n\n            if strongest_ext is None or current_ext.strength > strongest_ext.strength:\n                strongest_ext = current_ext\n            # Tie-breaking: if strengths are equal, the first one encountered is retained.\n            # This is implicitly handled as strongest_ext only updates on strictly greater strength.\n\n        # The input 'extensions' list is guaranteed not to be empty by specification.\n        return strongest_ext\n\n\ndef Strongest_Extension(class_name, extensions):\n    \"\"\"Finds the strongest extension and formats the output string.\"\"\"\n    calculator = ExtensionStrengthCalculator()\n    finder = StrongestExtensionFinder(calculator)\n    strongest_ext_obj = finder.find(extensions)\n\n    return f\"{class_name}.{strongest_ext_obj.name}\"\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/151", "solution": "```python\ndef double_the_difference(lst):\n    '''\n    Given a list of numbers, return the sum of squares of the numbers\n    in the list that are odd. Ignore numbers that are negative or not integers.\n    '''\n    \n    # Helper function to check if a value is an integer.\n    def _is_integer(num: object) -> bool:\n        return isinstance(num, int)\n\n    # Helper function to check if an integer is strictly positive.\n    def _is_positive(num: int) -> bool:\n        return num > 0\n\n    # Helper function to check if an integer is odd.\n    def _is_odd(num: int) -> bool:\n        return num % 2 != 0\n\n    total_sum = 0\n    for item in lst:\n        # Process item only if it's an odd, positive integer.\n        if _is_integer(item) and _is_positive(item) and _is_odd(item):\n            total_sum += item * item\n            \n    return total_sum\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/155", "solution": "```python\ndef even_odd_count(num):\n    \"\"\"Given an integer, return a tuple that has the number of even and odd digits respectively.\n    The sign of the input integer does not affect the even/odd count of its digits.\n    \"\"\"\n    even_count = 0\n    odd_count = 0\n\n    abs_num = abs(num)\n\n    if abs_num == 0:\n        return (1, 0)\n\n    num_str = str(abs_num)\n    for digit_char in num_str:\n        digit = int(digit_char)\n        if digit % 2 == 0:\n            even_count += 1\n        else:\n            odd_count += 1\n            \n    return (even_count, odd_count)\n```"}
