{"task_id": "HumanEval/153", "solution": "def Strongest_Extension(class_name, extensions):\n    \"\"\"\n    Identifies the strongest extension from a list and formats it with the class name.\n    Strength is calculated as (uppercase letters - lowercase letters).\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _calculate_strength(extension_name: str) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Calculates the strength of an extension string.\n        It counts uppercase letters (CAP) and lowercase letters (SM) to return CAP - SM.\n        \"\"\"\n        cap_count = sum(1 for char in extension_name if 'A' <= char <= 'Z')\n        sm_count = sum(1 for char in extension_name if 'a' <= char <= 'z')\n        return cap_count - sm_count\n\n    # If the list of extensions is empty, return the class name only as per design.\n    if not extensions:\n        return class_name\n\n    # Initialize the strongest extension with the first element to handle tie-breaking correctly.\n    strongest_ext_name = extensions[0]\n    max_strength = _calculate_strength(extensions[0])\n\n    # Iterate through the rest of the extensions to find the truly strongest one.\n    for ext_name in extensions[1:]:\n        current_strength = _calculate_strength(ext_name)\n        if current_strength > max_strength:\n            max_strength = current_strength\n            strongest_ext_name = ext_name\n            \n    # Format and return the result \"ClassName.StrongestExtensionName\".\n    return f\"{class_name}.{strongest_ext_name}\""}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/156", "solution": "```python\nROMAN_MAP = [\n    (1000, 'm'), (900, 'cm'), (500, 'd'), (400, 'cd'),\n    (100, 'c'), (90, 'xc'), (50, 'l'), (40, 'xl'),\n    (10, 'x'), (9, 'ix'), (5, 'v'), (4, 'iv'),\n    (1, 'i')\n]\n\ndef int_to_mini_roman(number):\n    \"\"\"\n    Given a positive integer, obtain its roman numeral equivalent as a string,\n    and return it in lowercase.\n    \"\"\"\n    roman_numeral = []\n    temp_num = number\n\n    for value, symbol in ROMAN_MAP:\n        while temp_num >= value:\n            roman_numeral.append(symbol)\n            temp_num -= value\n    \n    return \"\".join(roman_numeral)\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/157", "solution": "import math\n\nEPSILON = 1e-9\n\ndef right_angle_triangle(a, b, c):\n    '''\n    Given the lengths of the three sides of a triangle. Return True if the three\n    sides form a right-angled triangle, False otherwise.\n    A right-angled triangle is a triangle in which one angle is right angle or \n    90 degree.\n    '''\n    if not (a > 0 and b > 0 and c > 0):\n        return False\n\n    sides = sorted([a, b, c])\n    s1, s2, s3 = sides[0], sides[1], sides[2]\n\n    # Apply Pythagorean theorem for floating-point comparison.\n    return math.isclose(s1**2 + s2**2, s3**2, rel_tol=EPSILON)"}
